       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/628068f58d175962c7274ca5ca03993f?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FAS-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "A. Soroka",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A24c578cc-15e9-4649-9f68-5eace85735e0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Is it plausible to assemble a commons suite of error messages across SOAP and REST? If the two API instantiations truly run in parallel (which they do not, but which we would like them to) then this shouldn't be impossible. In fact, the exercise might help turn up differences that need be addressed.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
